  "problem": "The vertical asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{4x-8}{2{x}^{2}+2x-12}$ is\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-8}{2{x}^{2}+2x-12} & =\\frac{4(x-2)}{2(x+3)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cancel{(x-2)}}{2(x+3)\\cancel{(x-2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\nx+3=0\\,\u27f9\\,x=-3\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=-3.$",
